[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Queen's Pawn Game: London System, ...Qb6 and ...c4"]
[ECO "D02"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "b2-pressure,a-file"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2.Nf3 and 3.Bf4"]
[Start "orthodox 1...d5"]

2. Nf3 Nf6 { Develops a piece and guards d5 and e4, so White cannot easily push e4. } 3. Bf4 c5 { Hits d4 at once, before White has played e3 and c3 to protect it. The London bishop on f4 does not guard d4. } 4. e3 ( 4. c3 Nc6 5. e3 ) ( 4. dxc5 e6 5. e3 Bxc5 { Takes the pawn back, and the bishop develops with the capture. } ) ( 4. Nbd2 cxd4 { White has not played e3, so a pawn cannot retake on d4. A knight has to, and it is the centre pawn that disappears. } 5. Nxd4 Nbd7 ) 4... Nc6 { A second attacker on d4, and a piece developed. } 5. c3 Qb6 { Hits b2 and d4 together. The bishop left c1, so only the queen guards b2, and White has to react. } 6. Qb3 ( 6. Qc1 Nh5 { Attacks the bishop. If it retreats to g3, Black takes it with the knight and keeps both bishops against bishop and knight. } 7. Be5 cxd4 8. Bxd4 ) ( 6. Nbd2 cxd4 7. cxd4 Bf5 ) 6... c4 { Attacks the queen and grabs space. White must trade queens or retreat, and the pawn on c4 also stops White's bishop going to d3. } 7. Qxb6 ( 7. Qc2 Bf5 { The bishop comes out before ...e6 closes it in, and it attacks the queen on c2 again. } 8. Qc1 e6 ) 7... axb6 { The a-pawn recaptures, so the a-file opens for Black's rook and the knights stay where they are. } 8. Nbd2 Bf5 { Gets the bishop outside the pawn chain before ...e6 shuts it in. } 9. Be2 e6 { Guards d5 and opens the bishop on f8. } 10. O-O b5 { Backs up c4, so White cannot break the chain with e4. Castle after ...Be7, put a rook on the open a-file, and meet e4 with ...dxe4 and ...Nd5. } *
